        "original_id": "fea079c1-217a-5182-bea6-ed9ec7961b63",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: ESPN, ESPN2, NTRA\n- Events: Kentucky Derby, Preakness Stakes, Belmont Stakes, Breeders' Cup World Thoroughbred Championships, Kentucky Oaks, Black-Eyed Susan Stakes, Eclipse Awards, Kentucky Derby Festival\n- Programs: NTRA Racing to the Kentucky Derby, Road To The World Thoroughbred Championships/NTRA Racing to the Breeders' Cup, NTRA 2Day At the Races, Racing Across America, Long John Silver's Wire to Wire, RaceHorse Digest\n- Places: Louisville, Kentucky, United States\n- Topics: Thoroughbred racing\n\nFacts:\n- ESPN and ESPN2 aired Thoroughbred racing coverage that included NTRA Racing to the Kentucky Derby.\n- ESPN and ESPN2 aired Road To The World Thoroughbred Championships/NTRA Racing to the Breeders' Cup, a series of prep races for the Breeders' Cup World Thoroughbred Championships.\n- ESPN and ESPN2 covered the post position draws for the Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes.\n- ESPN and ESPN2 televised the Kentucky Derby and Belmont Stakes undercard races, the Preakness undercard races, the Kentucky Oaks, and the Black-Eyed Susan Stakes.\n- ESPN and ESPN2 aired NTRA 2Day At the Races, Racing Across America, and the Eclipse Awards show.\n- ESPN and ESPN2 aired Long John Silver's Wire to Wire, a weekly Thoroughbred racing magazine show that was previously known as RaceHorse Digest.\n- The Kentucky Derby is an annual horse race held in Louisville, Kentucky, United States, on the first Saturday in May.\n- The Kentucky Derby caps the two-week-long Kentucky Derby Festival.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5ff05075-5e72-509b-821b-90688a87deb6",
        "text": "Page: Thoroughbred Racing on ESPN. Sentence: ESPN and ESPN2's coverage of Thoroughbred racing consisted of NTRA Racing to the Kentucky Derby., Road To The World Thoroughbred Championships/NTRA Racing to the Breeders' Cup, a series of prep races for the Breeders' Cup World Thoroughbred Championships, the post position draw for the Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes, the Kentucky Derby and Belmont Stakes undercard races, the Kentucky Oaks and Black-Eyed Susan Stakes, NTRA 2Day At the Races, Racing Across America, the Preakness undercard races, the Eclipse Awards show, and Long John Silver's Wire to Wire (previously known as RaceHorse Digest), a weekly thoroughbred racing magazine show.\nPage: Kentucky Derby. Sentence: The Kentucky Derby is a horse race that is held annually in Louisville, Kentucky, United States, on the first Saturday in May, capping the two-week-long Kentucky Derby Festival.",
